  "body": {
    "id": "thm:fuzzy-nuisance-lower",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Suppose \\(0<s\\le1/2\\), \\(t<d/2\\), the Hölder balls contain the balanced two-outcome baseline in their interiors, and the fixed periodic kernel has \\(a_0>0\\) and ordered nonzero Fourier weights \\(a_{(j)}\\asymp j^{-2r}\\), with the declared covariance-profile constants wide enough to contain the derived sandwich in \\(\\mathrm{lem{:}fuzzy\\mbox{-}legality\\mbox{-}affinity}\\). Under uniform \\(P_X\\), \\(\\delta_n^\\star\\ge c n^{-2t/(2t+d)}\\) for a class constant \\(c>0\\). At \\(h=c_hn^{-2/(2t+d)}\\), every \\(P_\\omega\\) belongs to \\(\\mathcal M_0\\), every \\(Q_\\omega\\) belongs to \\(\\mathcal M_1(cn^{-2t/(2t+d)};s,R)\\), the one-record mixtures coincide exactly, and the \\(n\\)-record mixtures have affinity bounded away from zero. Hence \\(\\delta_n^\\star/\\delta_{n,e}^\\star\\to\\infty\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
